1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
From my score/chord editor
to an AI reharmonization agent.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Built for this hackathon with Muse Spark.
The editor and chord model came first.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Import a score PDF as editable chords.
The local reader opens it right away.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Muse Spark finishes its background check.
A confirmation appears above the score.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Play panel: switch parts, set the mix.
Hear the arrangement take shape.

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Reharmonize agent: up to four chords,
three alternatives to compare.

7
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,500
Muse Spark decides what to search
and calls the search tools.

8
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:07,000
My existing model scores each change;
Muse Spark offers three that differ.

9
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Meta run details: muse-spark-1.3,
request ids, cost and time.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Compare and combine the alternatives.
Apply the changes you want to keep.

11
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Let's check the chord chart.

12
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
DAW export: Harmony, Bass and Drums
open in Logic Pro as editable MIDI.

13
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Unleash your creativity in your DAW.

14
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,500
Why Muse Spark: reading chords from notes,
it matched 89.5%; my local analyzer 77.8%.

15
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:06,700
Less setup. More time to make your music.
